From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:15:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] mb/dell/sklkbl_desktops: Stay off after AC power loss
 when configured

The SCH5555 powers the board on as soon as AC power returns, whatever
the PCH's "sleep after power failure" bit says, so "Restore AC power
after loss" set to "Power off (S5)" or "Previous state" behaved like
"Power on (S0)". After an AC cut with "Power off (S5)" the PCH reported
both PWR_FLR and the sleep bit set, and nothing in PM1_STS showed a
power button press.

coreboot keeps that bit set exactly when the system should stay off
after a power failure: always for "Power off (S5)", and from shutdown
until the next boot for "Previous state". So when the power state saved
in romstage has PWR_FLR and the bit set, clear PWR_FLR and power off
again. Clearing PWR_FLR first means the next press of the power button
boots.

This runs after FSP-S: an S5 request from the bootblock was ignored
and left the board hanging, since the PCH can't enter S5 before memory
and silicon init.

Signed-off-by: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/mainboard/dell/sklkbl_desktops/ramstage.c | 27 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/dell/sklkbl_desktops/ramstage.c b/src/mainboard/dell/sklkbl_desktops/ramstage.c
index 93dd73ead6..b62a78abac 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/dell/sklkbl_desktops/ramstage.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/dell/sklkbl_desktops/ramstage.c
@@ -4,9 +4,14 @@
 #include <acpi/acpigen.h>
 #include <bootstate.h>
 #include <arch/cpuid.h>
+#include <console/console.h>
 #include <cpu/x86/msr.h>
+#include <halt.h>
+#include <intelblocks/pmclib.h>
 #include <option.h>
 #include <soc/gpio.h>
+#include <soc/pm.h>
+#include <soc/pmc.h>
 #include <soc/ramstage.h>
 #include "../../../include/variant/gpio.h"
 #include <superio/smsc/sch555x/sch555x.h>
@@ -536,3 +541,25 @@ static void sch5555_ec_hwm_init(void *arg)
 }
 
 BOOT_STATE_INIT_ENTRY(BS_POST_DEVICE, BS_ON_EXIT, sch5555_ec_hwm_init, NULL);
+
+/*
+ * The SCH5555 powers the board on whenever AC power returns, ignoring the PCH's
+ * "sleep after power failure" bit, which coreboot sets while the system should
+ * stay off. Power off again, after FSP-S: the PCH can't enter S5 before memory
+ * and silicon init.
+ */
+static void sch5555_ac_recovery(void *arg)
+{
+	const struct chipset_power_state *ps = pmc_get_power_state();
+
+	if (!ps || !(ps->gen_pmcon_b & PWR_FLR) || !(ps->gen_pmcon_b & SLEEP_AFTER_POWER_FAIL))
+		return;
+
+	printk(BIOS_INFO, "AC power returned, staying off as configured\n");
+
+	/* Clear PWR_FLR, so the next power button press boots. */
+	pmc_clear_pmcon_pwr_failure_sts();
+	poweroff();
+}
+
+BOOT_STATE_INIT_ENTRY(BS_DEV_INIT_CHIPS, BS_ON_EXIT, sch5555_ac_recovery, NULL);
